meta {
  name: email-links
  seq: 25
}

docs {
  Manual test of the verify and cancel links. Every request here skips itself unless bruno/.env contains RUN_EMAIL_LINKS=true, so a normal collection run never touches them: the tokens only exist in the emails, and they work for one test only.

  The emails must reach a real inbox (.test addresses are skipped by the backend), so the bookings here are created for EMAIL_LINKS_TO.

  To run them, one at a time and in order:
  1. Add RUN_EMAIL_LINKS=true and EMAIL_LINKS_TO=<your address> to bruno/.env, and send "Login - admin" for adminToken.
  2. Send request 0 and copy the token at the end of the verify link in the email into bruno/.env as VERIFY_TOKEN (it lasts 30 minutes).
  3. Send requests 1 and 2. Request 2 sends the confirmation email: copy its cancel token into bruno/.env as CANCEL_TOKEN.
  4. Send requests 3 to 8.
  5. Big group withdrawn: send request 9, copy the token of the notice email's link as PENDING_CANCEL_TOKEN, then send 10 to 12.
  6. Big group rejected: send request 13, copy the token of the notice email's link as REJECTED_CANCEL_TOKEN, then send 14 to 16.
  7. Remove RUN_EMAIL_LINKS from bruno/.env, or the next full run will fail on the used tokens.

  Request 1 sets maxOnlineTables to 0 and back to 36 inside one single request: there is no separate setup request that could run alone.
  This folder saves 3 bookings: with the rest of the collection (5), still under the POST limit of 10 per IP every 15 minutes.
}
